  "reproducibility_frictions_observed": [
    "the paper prints no per-cell table and released no per-model result file: Figure 3 is the only original value, and the Codabench leaderboard the card offered as an alternative holds zero submissions. The comparison here rests on a vector digitisation of Figure 3 (columns 1-2 are a bar chart, so the SVG carries every bar); it happens to be exact - each value has a unique integer pre-image over the Table 5 denominators and the plotted Wald bars confirm it - but only because the figure was published as SVG, which is luck, not a reproducibility practice",
    "the frozen Codabench release is not downloadable anonymously (the Files tab requires a logged-in account; the public_data dataset endpoint returns HTTP 403), so the benchmark was regenerated in-repo and could not be diffed against the official release",
    "accord/io.py save_lines() appends os.linesep in text mode, which doubles the CR on Windows and makes every one of the repository's own loaders raise JSONDecodeError on its own output; the generator cannot run on Windows without forcing os.linesep to '\\n'",
    "SimpleQACheckpointManager keys on a checkpoint directory whose default job_id is -1, so the README's own command sequence silently no-ops after the first QAData-iterating step (and writes checkpoints into the clone); each step here gets its own checkpoint directory",
    "requirements.txt pins coma>=1.0.1 but PyPI now serves coma 3.0.1, whose API dropped register/initiate/forget: src/main.py does not even import on a fresh install; coma==1.0.1 (2022) had to be pinned by hand",
    "accord.commands imports plotly at package import although the benchmarking path draws no figure; plotly is stubbed",
    "the answer prompt is surfaced with the instruction blanked (arguments/gpt-4o-2024-05-13.txt), so the user turn starts with an empty first surfacer and a leading newline - reproduced verbatim rather than tidied",
    "statement order is fixed by the sequencer's shuffles under random_seed 314159 and frozen into the snapshot; it is reproducible only because that seed is pinned, and it cannot be verified against the authors' own 2024 ordering",
    "temperature is the API default 1.0 with a best-effort seed, so the original single run is itself one draw; 3 complete seeds were run and the median is judged"
  ]
}